WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:01.600
(piano music)

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.200
- So I've talked on this channel before

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.430
about how I think there
are a lot of parallels

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.990
between video games and real life.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:08.990
In a video game,

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.260
as your character
progresses through the game

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.970
and you upgrade your stats

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.010
and make more money,

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.170
you're able to unlock better equipment,

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.480
new and more powerful abilities.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.740
And travel to different

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.740
and more exciting parts of the map.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.060
And life kind of works

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.630
in the exact same way.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.080
As you develop marketable skills

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.600
and improve yourself,

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.540
your options in life open up.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.840
Our entire society seems to operate

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.950
on a competence hierarchy.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.810
The people who get the most attention,

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:37.700
the most money,

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.710
and have the most opportunity in life,

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.410
tend to, not always,

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.080
but tend to be very,
very good at something.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.580
But everyone kind of knows this

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.140
whether instinctually

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.210
or by societal conditioning.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.217
So I'm not really saying
anything new like,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.757
"Oh, if you wanna get better at life

00:00:52.757 --> 00:00:53.747
"and be successful,

00:00:53.747 --> 00:00:56.237
"then stop playing so many video games

00:00:56.237 --> 00:00:57.307
"and spending so much time

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.127
"upgrading your video game character,

00:00:59.127 --> 00:01:02.030
"and start upgrading your
real life character."

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.580
While that may be true,

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.730
there's a glaring issue
with that whole approach.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.563
And it's that

00:01:07.563 --> 00:01:09.170
unlike video games,

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.420
upgrading your skills

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.470
and getting so good at things

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.410
to the point where people start paying you

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:15.243
lots of money,

00:01:15.243 --> 00:01:17.910
and you reach the upper
echelons of society,

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.890
if that's what you want to do anyways,

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.290
it's really hard to do.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:23.030
And it takes a lot of time.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:24.440
Years and years and years,

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.930
sometimes even decades.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:27.860
So people don't bother doing it.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.110
Pretty much everybody

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.960
knows exactly what it will take

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.280
to become successful,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.730
but it's just so difficult to do it

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.920
that we distract ourselves with TV

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.260
and video games

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.260
and whatever other vice that we have.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.760
So we stay in a bad situation

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.440
or a lower paying job

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:48.080
or whatever our undesirable
present conundrum is.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:48.913
But thankfully,

00:01:48.913 --> 00:01:49.970
I think there's an answer

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:50.930
to this problem.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.930
I think we can analyze video games

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.050
and try to figure out

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:56.070
what makes them so compelling.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:57.820
Why is it so fun to level up

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.170
our in game character?

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.300
And can we leverage that

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.910
and apply that same approach

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:03.780
to real life?

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:04.700
But in order to answer

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.520
that question more accurately,

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.580
we need to dive into video games

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.150
and figure out what video games

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.610
are doing better

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.794
than real life.

00:02:12.794 --> 00:02:15.294
(piano music)

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.420
Video games have better clarity

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.560
of objectives.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.610
Say in "Rune Scape"

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.790
if you're level one attack,

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.620
you can only wheel the
bronze or iron sword.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.420
And if you try to pick up a steel sword,

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.253
it won't let you.

00:02:28.253 --> 00:02:29.940
It says you need level five attack.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.570
So all you got to do is slash up goblins

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:33.570
for like half an hour,

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.180
and you can achieve level five.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.870
Even when you talk to a
random NPC in "Skyrim"

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.660
and he wants you to go do something,

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:40.730
whatever he said

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.300
automatically gets updated to a quest log.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.140
And if you were to Wikipedia that quest,

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.190
it would tell you

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.040
exactly what reward you stand to gain

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.150
from completing it

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.310
and what exact steps you need to do

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:53.630
to complete that quest.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:54.760
While the possibilities

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.300
for what you can do in a video game

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.080
may not be as extensive

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.390
as they are in real life,

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.880
the objectives are certainly more clear.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.730
We know exactly what we need to do

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:04.670
in a video game

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:05.550
most of the time,

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:06.700
unless it's a puzzle game

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:07.810
and you like that kind of thing.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.240
You usually have a backlog

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.570
of things you need to do.

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:11.800
And all the little steps

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:12.633
you need to get there

00:03:12.633 --> 00:03:15.380
are broken down into
little tiny baby steps

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.180
that will ensue towards your goal.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.170
In real life though,

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.440
you're kind of born to a random family,

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:21.810
in a random part of the map,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.030
you have a random race

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.810
and a random socioeconomic class.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:26.780
And as far as you know,

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.070
you didn't even agree

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.120
to play the game.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:29.953
You didn't even know

00:03:29.953 --> 00:03:30.786
you were playing the game

00:03:30.786 --> 00:03:33.800
until you gained some
sort of mental autonomy.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:34.633
You're kind of like,

00:03:34.633 --> 00:03:35.757
"Okay, I'm here now.

00:03:35.757 --> 00:03:37.707
"And my dad does this for a living.

00:03:37.707 --> 00:03:39.477
"And I have two siblings

00:03:39.477 --> 00:03:41.080
"and blahbity, blahbity, blah."

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:41.913
You're not really given

00:03:41.913 --> 00:03:43.230
a clear cut tutorial

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.970
as to what to do

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.320
or what the point of the game is.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.640
You kind of just arrived

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.293
and are expected to figure it out.

00:03:50.293 --> 00:03:51.850
The people around you

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.967
espouse vague sentiments like,

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.267
"Get a good job.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.467
"Find a good wife.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:58.610
"Settle down and have a nice house."

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:00.760
And all of these things are great,

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.920
but they definitely lack the clarity

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.287
that a video game gives you.

00:04:04.287 --> 00:04:06.140
And the vagueness of it all

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.220
definitely leads a lot of people

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.250
to have analysis paralysis,

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.550
or not know exactly what
they wanna do in life

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.050
because there's so many options,

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.230
they can't pick one.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.090
They're afraid if they go on a path,

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.470
it's not gonna be the right one.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.070
So video games definitely

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.770
have more clear objectives

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:24.523
that help you do stuff.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.990
Another big one is difficulty.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.940
Video games are way easier than real life.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:32.920
Physically, all it asks of you

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.610
is to move your fingers a little bit

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.040
and hit some plastic

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.100
every once in a while.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:38.933
All you're doing

00:04:38.933 --> 00:04:40.870
is kind of tricking your monkey brain

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:42.830
into thinking that
you're achieving things.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.663
But in reality,

00:04:43.663 --> 00:04:44.640
you're just sitting there.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:45.473
So physically,

00:04:45.473 --> 00:04:46.840
it's extremely easy.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.200
And the time commitment
is usually way lower.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.033
In "The Sims"

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.890
if you wanna become a master chef,

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.770
then it only takes like what?

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.280
A couple of weeks in game

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.113
or something like that,

00:04:57.113 --> 00:04:58.120
which really translates

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.810
to a couple of hours of playing.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:00.643
But in real life,

00:05:00.643 --> 00:05:02.150
if you wanna become a master chef,

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.920
it takes an entire lifetime.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:04.753
And not only that,

00:05:04.753 --> 00:05:06.630
you have to be interested in it.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.500
You have to be willing

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:11.260
to sacrifice friendships and other things

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.750
in order to pursue that goal

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.210
over years and years

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.360
and decades.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.950
- Roll the (beep) pizza dough.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.480
- [Man] Here's more mozzarella.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.660
- Roll the (beep) pizza dough.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:21.493
What are you doing?

00:05:21.493 --> 00:05:23.290
- You wanna find a wife in "The Sims"

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:24.123
all you have to do

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:26.070
is look around for the first girl

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:26.903
that you see

00:05:26.903 --> 00:05:29.340
that's kind of this
relatively same age as you

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.820
and you woo her.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.600
Spam the flirt options

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.300
until her attracted to you bar goes up?

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.550
Anyways, there's literally a bar

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.000
that tells you how into you she is.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.660
And as soon as that bar hits the end

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:42.750
or it max's out,

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:43.920
you can pop her the question

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.010
and then you have a wife.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.280
And that can take like 15 minutes to do.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.240
In real life though,

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.900
if you wanna find a spouse,

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.700
you got to clean yourself up a bit.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.600
You have to be somewhat respectable.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:54.690
You got to go out

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.100
and meet new people

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.830
and put yourself in
uncomfortable situations.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.790
You have to be bold and courageous

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.060
to ask people out

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:03.190
and ask them on a date.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.900
And you need to show up to that date.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.650
You need to be on time for that date.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:07.870
You need to be engaged

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:08.750
and listen.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.220
You need to ask difficult questions.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.770
You need to see if that person

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:14.860
is actually somewhat like you,

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:16.250
or if you guys can relate.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:17.230
And maybe that will lead to

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:18.210
a couple more dates.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.890
And it might work out in heartbreak

00:06:19.890 --> 00:06:21.330
because you really liked that girl

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.510
and she didn't like you back.

00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:23.980
Or maybe she really liked you

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.250
and you didn't really like her,

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.720
and you had to tell her the hard truth

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:27.950
that you're just not into her.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.590
There's a lot of emotional stakes

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:31.170
and uncomfortable situations

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:32.480
that go into dating

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.740
and potentially finding a spouse.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:35.573
And a lot of the time

00:06:35.573 --> 00:06:36.406
that whole process

00:06:36.406 --> 00:06:39.060
can take several iterations.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.190
You can be going on dates

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:41.450
for years and years

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:42.690
and decades even.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.620
And you might never even find a spouse.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:45.620
Who knows?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:46.500
It's not math.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:47.850
It's not like in video games

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:49.500
where there's a little algorithm

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:50.350
you have to follow

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:52.670
or you do a little Wikipedia search

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.503
for something.

00:06:53.503 --> 00:06:56.910
Life is just way harder than video games.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.170
Even if you look at something so simple

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:01.050
as getting jacked,

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:03.590
getting big and muscular at the gym.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:04.540
In real life,

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.080
it's actually pretty simple.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.510
Eat lots of protein,

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:10.350
around a gram per pound of body weight.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.520
You need to go to the gym

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.660
and lift more weight

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.120
than you did last time.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:14.953
You got to do that

00:07:14.953 --> 00:07:16.100
over and over and over again

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:19.050
until you're just a huge human being.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:20.310
But in most video games,

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:22.000
your characters usually just come

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.400
prebuilt jacked.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.310
You're just a super muscular guy

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.297
right off the get-go,

00:07:26.297 --> 00:07:27.830
and you don't even need to workout

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:28.663
to maintain it.

00:07:28.663 --> 00:07:29.496
It's amazing.

00:07:29.496 --> 00:07:30.660
- [Man] It's my ideal form.

00:07:31.878 --> 00:07:33.911
I'm just freaking jacked

00:07:33.911 --> 00:07:35.093
and I'm yoked.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:38.710
- So let's talk about risk,

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:39.750
not the board game,

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.740
but the concept of risk.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:43.690
In real life,

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.090
everything is kind of a risk.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.430
In the pursuit of wealth,

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:48.170
you risk going bankrupt.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.620
In the pursuit of intimacy,

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.010
we risk rejection.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:53.370
In the pursuit of a particular degree,

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:54.670
you risk the chance

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.490
that you picked the wrong one.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.210
You risk years of hating

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.350
whatever you picked.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.620
But in video games,

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:02.500
there's basically no risk.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.230
You risk losing gold
and supplies, I guess,

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:07.800
that don't really exist.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.930
But ultimately, you don't get to feel

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:12.530
the stabs, the hacks and the slashes

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:14.840
inflicted upon your end game character.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:15.810
If you die,

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.100
you just respond.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.790
If your team gets squad wiped,

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.260
you just play another round.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.093
In video games,

00:08:21.093 --> 00:08:22.550
you get all of the reward

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:24.060
with none of the risk.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.800
So video games have clearer objectives.

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:28.250
They are easier to do.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.860
And there's basically no risk involved.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.850
Then what's stopping us from spending

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:34.720
just all of our time in video games

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:36.700
and giving up on this whole life thing

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.150
and just spending all of our time

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:39.220
playing "Minecraft"

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.460
Well, I think it's in this final category

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.760
where life really takes the lead.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.198
And that is the category of rewards.

00:08:46.198 --> 00:08:48.010
(upbeat music)

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:50.160
It's nice to get a little dopamine rush

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.360
when you get a headshot

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.090
or a squad wipe or a win

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.720
or unlocking that new armor

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:55.990
or that special knife.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:57.020
But it only feels good

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.710
while you're playing the game.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:01.120
Video game rewards are what I would call,

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.610
superficial rewards.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.260
They're instantly gratifying,

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.620
kind of like a donut.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.453
They're sweet

00:09:06.453 --> 00:09:08.340
and they're colorful on the surface,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.220
but hollow

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:11.860
and nutritionally useless at its core.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:12.720
At their core?

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:13.553
At their core.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:15.120
And if all you eat is donuts,

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.660
you will gradually decay

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.560
and become ill

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:18.920
on a long enough timeline.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.790
Video game rewards are fun,

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:22.980
but they do virtually nothing

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:26.210
to increase your baseline
sense of fulfillment.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:28.220
Whereas rewards in real life,

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.900
both have a higher ceiling

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:32.430
and are deeper and longer lasting.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:33.800
You don't need me to tell you

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.150
that there's kind of a difference

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:36.500
in the reward you get

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.860
from unlocking a new
helmet in a video game

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.450
versus the rewards you get

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.040
for being a good father

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.770
and raising a family

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.660
and instilling good
values into your children.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:47.780
Getting a squad wipe

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:49.640
is really fun in the moment,

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:51.350
but it pales in comparison

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:53.320
to the type of satisfaction

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.610
that living a life

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.470
that you're proud of gives you.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.540
Being somebody that you admire.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.550
Living your life in a way that,

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:01.770
if you were viewing yourself

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:02.760
from the third person,

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.230
you'd say, "Hey, that
guy's a really cool guy."

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:08.440
Being that person offers
you a satisfaction

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:11.430
that video game rewards
just can't give you.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.270
Life offers you the opportunity

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.280
to make something of yourself

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.660
so you can contribute
to the world around you.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:20.210
And that feels good on
an existential level,

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:22.540
not just on a little brain chemical level.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:23.950
So that's kind of enough of that

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.350
Sunday school sermon.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.700
How do we make real life

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.050
into a video game?

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.600
How do we leech all of the power

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.500
and the compelling nature of video games

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.080
and apply it to real life?

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.860
Well, I have a couple ideas.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:37.800
Well, a few ideas.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:38.660
A couple is two.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.550
A few is more than three?

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:41.383
Three or more?

00:10:41.383 --> 00:10:42.400
I have a few ideas,

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.570
several ideas even.

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:47.030
Step one is to get clearer objectives.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.120
You have to treat the goals in your life

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:50.260
like a quest log

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.400
in a video game.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.080
You have to clearly define

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:54.520
what your goal is

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.220
and what the steps you need to take

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.370
to get there are.

00:10:57.370 --> 00:10:58.920
And then you need to clearly define

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.740
the reward that you stand to gain

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:02.310
for achieving that thing.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.050
If you don't have that roadmap,

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.660
then you can't really guarantee

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.840
that your brain can fully understand

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:09.090
what's at stake.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:11.410
It's just gonna become
another vague sentiment

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:13.640
that gets brushed under the rug

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.430
and you ignore for your whole life.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.400
So if something is important to you,

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.233
write it down.

00:11:18.233 --> 00:11:19.680
Write exactly what it is

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.000
that you need to achieve.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.020
And write down every single little step

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:24.690
you need to take to get there

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.360
as efficiently as possible.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:27.440
And then you can get yourself

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.720
emotionally excited about it.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.120
There's a reason why you want

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.170
the things that you want.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.003
It's because

00:11:33.003 --> 00:11:35.320
you stand to gain so much from it.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:37.310
But unless you clearly define it,

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:38.310
you're going to forget it.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:40.140
And once you create a roadmap

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:42.600
of all of the quests you have on cue,

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.070
you could really benefit from reducing

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.090
the difficulty.

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.480
Video games are extremely easy.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:49.400
Life is hard.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.060
But it doesn't have to be that way.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.660
You can break down these quests

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.800
into the smallest possible daily action

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.760
that will propel you towards your goal.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:00.280
If your goal is to write a book,

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.820
and you've always wanted to write a book,

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.710
you wanna to become an author,

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.300
then break down that thing, that goal,

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.770
into this smallest possible daily habit

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.690
that you're actually likely to do.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:12.410
And that's probably something like

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.370
write 100 words a day.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.970
And that might be so insultingly low,

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:17.817
you'll think to yourself,

00:12:17.817 --> 00:12:19.557
"Wow, I'll never achieve

00:12:19.557 --> 00:12:20.987
"the goal of writing a book.

00:12:20.987 --> 00:12:22.610
"100 words. That's nothing."

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.980
But if you usually do zero words,

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:27.180
that's infinitely more than zero.

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.013
I think that's math.

00:12:28.013 --> 00:12:28.846
I was about to say

00:12:28.846 --> 00:12:30.340
it's 100 times more than zero.

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:32.410
But that's just 100% not true.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.040
If you want to learn guitar,

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.900
if you wanna be very good at guitar,

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.420
but you never practice,

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:39.010
then download a habit tracker

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:41.490
and make "practice 15 minutes of guitar"

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.930
I don't know how many quotations I need,

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:43.810
a daily habit

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:45.480
that you do every single day.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:46.507
And you might think to yourself,

00:12:46.507 --> 00:12:47.797
"Wow, 15 minutes?

00:12:47.797 --> 00:12:48.777
"Everybody that I know

00:12:48.777 --> 00:12:49.867
"who's very good at guitar

00:12:49.867 --> 00:12:52.200
"practices for at least an hour a day."

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.200
Well, you don't.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.400
And you need to get in the habit

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.170
and get really good at practicing

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:57.210
15 minutes a day

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.800
over the period of months

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.250
before you upgrade to 20 minutes,

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.360
30 minutes,

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.700
40 minutes even.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:04.640
So the next thing

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:07.210
is for things that remain difficult

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:08.240
no matter what.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.110
Not everything can be broken down

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:11.500
into a tiny little habit

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:14.150
that you take action on every single day.

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:16.490
Some things are just acutely difficult

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:18.020
and you have to deal with them.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.660
So there's a weird phenomenon

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.690
I've noticed throughout my whole life.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:22.523
And that is

00:13:22.523 --> 00:13:25.000
that you can game-ify resistance.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:26.950
There's power to be absorbed

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:28.940
from the feeling of resistance.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.690
If you've ever gone cliff jumping,

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.600
then you know this feeling really well.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.400
All your friends are jumping off

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.480
of this 30 foot cliff into the water.

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:38.090
They're having such a good time time.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:39.160
And it's your turn.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:40.320
And you hate Heights.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.000
As you step onto that ledge,

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:44.020
there's a feeling in your gut.

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:45.800
It's like this tight knot.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.280
All of your survival instincts

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:49.200
are telling you not to jump.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:50.450
There is like a wall,

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.360
a palpable wall of resistance

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:55.860
stopping you from taking that leap.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.090
But if you've ever taken that leap before,

00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.350
you know that the second

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.160
your foot leaves that ledge,

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.440
you ignore the resistance anyways.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:05.410
There's almost a euphoria

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.730
that overwhelms you

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:08.680
as you jump over the cliff

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:11.130
and you plunge into that icy cold water.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:14.050
You feel alive and invigorated.

00:14:14.050 --> 00:14:16.810
You feel incredible and powerful.

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:18.320
It's because you absorbed

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:20.760
the power of that resistance.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:21.680
You devoured it.

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.200
And this applies to pretty much

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:24.130
everything in life

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.950
where there is a significant amount

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:27.460
of internal resistance.

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:29.160
When you overcome resistance,

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.630
you absorb its power.

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:32.430
And the greater the resistance,

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.570
the greater the power.

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.270
And understanding this truth

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.770
can really change the way

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.130
that you see the world.

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.090
Instead of seeing it as a bad thing

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.780
that the rewards in life

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:44.290
are hidden behind discomfort paywalls,

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:45.550
you'll view it as a good thing.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:47.640
You'll see these pockets of discomfort

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:48.650
as power-ups

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:50.970
that you can absorb on demand.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:52.620
They're lying around everywhere

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.780
for you in life.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:54.880
Asking a girl out,

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:57.450
there'll be a wall of discomfort there.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.260
But overcoming that wall

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:00.830
offers you the power,

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.310
regardless of the response.

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:04.780
She could reject you or whatever,

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:06.150
but it doesn't take away the fact

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.970
that you overcame discomfort

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.940
and you have become somebody

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:12.210
who is better at overcoming discomfort.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:13.830
And that is a tangible,

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.410
powerful feeling to have.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.090
And it's a power that sticks with you.

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:19.200
So game-ify discomfort.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:21.170
And another way to game-ify real life

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.000
is to embrace risk.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.810
If you become a risk taker,

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:27.610
somebody who's more comfortable with risk,

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:28.980
you'll gain the strength

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.540
to bear life's pain.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.580
Realize that by not taking risks in life,

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.850
you're not saving yourself from pain.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:37.790
All you're doing is trading away

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.310
the acute discomfort of action

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:44.090
for the slow burning longer lasting decay

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:45.040
of inaction,

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.350
where feelings like
despair and regret blossom.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:50.280
So how is that any less painful?

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.113
And the final thing

00:15:51.113 --> 00:15:52.350
is just to remind yourself

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:54.130
and reflect on the rewards

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:55.870
that life has to offer.

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.290
You're allowed to get excited

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:00.630
about being the person
that you want to be.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:01.463
Achieving something

00:16:01.463 --> 00:16:03.090
you've always wanted to achieve.

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:04.210
And I think it's important

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:07.740
that we reflect on these
potential rewards often.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:10.470
Otherwise, our daily grind can kind of

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.280
get so monotonous

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.600
it feels pointless.

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:15.930
One reward that I'm currently aspiring

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.330
to achieve right now

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:20.960
is less of a tangible physical reward,

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:22.570
but more of a feeling.

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:24.980
The feeling of sort of calm

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.850
and peacefulness

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.680
and tranquility.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.810
And I want to invite that feeling

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:32.040
into my life

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:33.300
as much as possible.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:34.720
I'm going camping this weekend

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.240
so I'm really looking forward

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:39.400
to just letting all of the worries of life

00:16:40.788 --> 00:16:41.720
(beep) off for a bit

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:44.130
so that I can just be
at peace with myself.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.310
And I know for a fact

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:47.510
that's a feeling that video games

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:48.550
can't really give me.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.000
There's a reason why
people play video games.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:51.960
They're super fun.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.080
They're super compelling.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.490
But the video game rewards

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.970
pale in comparison to

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.070
the type of rewards

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.170
that life can give you

00:16:58.170 --> 00:16:59.610
when it starts going your way.

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:01.150
And if it feels like it's been a while

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:02.690
since it's been going your way,

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:04.150
I hope at least that this video

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:05.380
has given you some ideas

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.200
you can sink your teeth into

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:09.200
so you start feeling better really soon.

